# Where every trained spot's picture comes from

D404. A trained spot is a place in a game where the Anti-Recoil Lab's
Automatic does everything by itself: the Core checks the player stands
there, aims, fires one magazine, times the fire rate and finds the holes.
Each spot in a game pack (`recoilSpots`) names one picture in this folder,
which players see on the spot card ("stand here, face the wall like this").

Rules: real frames only. Every picture here is the Core's own capture of
the game, taken by **Train this spot** (developer builds) at the moment the
owner captured the spot's view. Never a screenshot from the web, never a
drawn or generated picture.

These pictures live in the app only: the exe and the phone app carry this
folder, and no picture is ever sent to or kept on the Core (the spot's
48 x 27 reference thumbnail is sent for one Lab session and forgotten).

`dashboard/tools/add-recoil-spot.js` copies a picture in and adds its row
below. `dashboard/tools/test-game-packs.js` fails a spot whose picture is
missing or not listed.

